description: MCP server source for JSON-RPC envelope handling, tool dispatch, and compiler/runtime composition
includes:
  - crates/sigil-mcp/src/
excludes:
  - crates/sigil-mcp/target/
context: |
  This scope is the implementation-level view of the MCP server. Edits here
  cover JSON-RPC framing, tool argument parsing, and how requests fan out
  into `sigil-compiler` and `sigil-runtime` calls.

  Keep this layer thin and translation-only: parse the request envelope,
  validate arguments, invoke the right compiler/runtime API, marshal the
  response. Language semantics, diagnostic content, or runtime behavior
  belong in the underlying crates — not here.

  Pass ordering inside a request:
  parse JSON-RPC envelope -> dispatch on method (initialize / tools/list /
  tools/call) -> for tools/call, dispatch on tool name -> parse tool args ->
  call into compiler or runtime -> serialize a tool-shaped JSON response.

  Current hygiene expectations:
  - keep the protocol contract stable: any change to the envelope shape
    (the `data` keys, error codes, `output_text`/`output_bytes`/`fuel_consumed`
    placement) is a breaking change for every agent harness
  - integration tests in `crates/sigil-mcp/tests/protocol.rs` spawn the real
    binary and exercise this exactly — treat their assertions as the
    boundary contract
  - error codes follow JSON-RPC 2.0: -32601 method-not-found, -32602
    invalid-params, -32603 internal-error
  - protocol version is pinned at the top of `main.rs` (`PROTOCOL_VERSION`);
    changes require coordinated agent-harness updates

  Current implemented surface (all in `main.rs`, no submodules):
  - `handle_initialize` / `handle_tools_list` — MCP handshake + capability
    advertisement
  - `tool_sigil_check` — compile via `compile_named_module`, emit diagnostics
    JSON
  - `tool_sigil_forge` — compile via `compile_tool`, then `execute_ephemeral`
    with caller-supplied `IoGrants` (fuel, network, filesystem); the source
    must export the canonical `tool_main` entry point
  - `tool_sigil_lookup_error` — query the diagnostics `registry`
  - `tool_sigil_inspect_uses` — parser-only path that surfaces `use` decls
    without running the full compile pipeline (advisory; bench harness uses
    this for stdlib-usage checks)
related:
  - crates/sigil-mcp/.scope
  - crates/sigil-abi/.scope
  - crates/sigil-compiler/.scope
  - crates/sigil-runtime/.scope
tags:
  - mcp
  - src
  - json-rpc
  - agent
